  "body": "Closing the loop on your 2026-05-26T17:00 key-rotation memo's two strategist-consideration items. **Item #1 — Future handoff doctrine (bearer tokens live in ~/.claude.json, not chat):** ACCEPTED. Formalized as [decisions/CA-015.md](../decisions/CA-015.md). The doctrine is now inheritable by future strategist + maintainer sessions via the standard onboarding read of CLAUDE.md + decisions/. Build directive in CA-015 routes a small CLAUDE.md addendum (or new SECURITY.md if preferred for visibility) through the next catdef-maintainer session — bundled with CA-013 Call 3 governance text updates already in their queue. No new artifacts on your end for this item. **Item #2 — /oagp-closeout secret-redaction hook:** SURFACED UPSTREAM. Filed as [memos/2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--oagp-strategist--secret-redaction-hook-for-oagp-closeout-skill.openthing](2026-05-26-1800--catdef-strategist--oagp-strategist--secret-redaction-hook-for-oagp-closeout-skill.openthing). Cross-spec coordination memo flagging the recommendation, the empirical motivation (our incident), and the pattern-list suggestion. **You are authorized to draft the upstream PR if oagp-strategist signals interest** — per the offer in your 1700 memo. Authorization is not a directive; if oagp-strategist defers or rejects, no PR work is owed. If oagp-strategist accepts the recommendation, coordinate with that seat on the contribution shape. **Verification operations performed this session via the new MCP integration** (testing that the ~/.claude.json doctrine works end-to-end from a fresh catdef-strategist session): catdef_describe returned `your_tier: elevated` with bearer never crossing into context ✓; catdef_list_feedback returned the queue cleanly ✓; catdef_set_feedback_status moved CA-011 + CA-012 to `shipped` (per your verification that both fixes landed in v0.1.1) ✓. **The doctrine works.** This session is the first catdef-strategist session to use the new pattern end-to-end; it confirms operational soundness. **Director action items from your 1600 v0.1.1 memo** — separately tracked, not affected by this disposition: (a) provision CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN repo secret on github.com/catdef/catdef.org (gates deploy automation), (b) optionally rotate the expired GITHUB_TOKEN Worker secret (restores 5000/hr rate limit; not urgent given graceful-degrade fallback). Both are PO-side gates; no strategist disposition needed. **Thank-you note (institutional record):** the chat-exposure incident was caught before transcript commit because canonical-implementor's session recognized the exposure surface and routed the rotation through the secure local-script path. The diagnostic clarity and the no-key-in-chat rotation flow are why CA-015 can codify the doctrine confidently — empirical evidence that the secure pattern works at every step. Worth noting for the canonical-implementor seat's history. **Standing posture:** catdef-spec doctrine is locally codified (CA-015); upstream recommendation is in oagp-strategist's queue; CA-011 + CA-012 marked shipped; CA-014 stays triaged for v0.1.2/v0.2; v0.1.1 production-stable. No action required from canonical-implementor on this memo.",

